{"aligned_passages":[{"anchor":"invariants","mapping_field":"claim_ids","mapping_ref":"sha256:57d520f131d63518eaab4bc49e02c1466414e4aa6afcee1b9cabfc26bbc1f419/papers/long.json","paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/long?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765","passage_ref":"sha256:f7c2487ba172be55e583becc143742c2d34c576d0d1339fd730197a0c97bb374/papers/long.md/sha256:57d520f131d63518eaab4bc49e02c1466414e4aa6afcee1b9cabfc26bbc1f419/papers/long.json/passages/invariants","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&paper=long&passage=invariants","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&paper=long&passage=invariants","span":{"end_byte":243276,"end_line":2799,"start_byte":213673,"start_line":2408},"stage":"long"}],"lenses":{"consumers":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&view=arguments&node=long.record-257hg-i4&direction=consumers&assumptions=true","direct_passages":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&node=long.record-257hg-i4&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&node=long.record-257hg-i4&relation=prerequisites","prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&view=arguments&node=long.record-257hg-i4&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&ref=sha256%3A264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c%2Fnodes%2Flong.record-257hg-i4","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"The evidence mapping records a Lean proof of exactly this statement. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.record-257hg-i4"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257hg-i4"],"id":"long.record-257hg-i4","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.120 (A sufficient inequality for a safe skip)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.120, p. 77, label record:257hg-i4","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Let $k,u,L\\ge1$ be integers, set $a=2L-(2^k-1)u$, and suppose $a>0$. For the skipped rational remainder $\\rho=u/(2L)$, $\\rho\\le2^{-k}$ is equivalent to $u\\le a$, whereas\n$$\n2u\\le3a\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\\rho<R_k.\n$$\nThe latter implication uses the three-term lower bound above. More explicitly, with $t=2^k\\ge2$,\n$$\n\\left(\\frac1t+\\frac1{3t^2}+\\frac1{7t^3}\\right)\n       -\\frac3{3t-1}\n =\\frac{2t-3}{21t^3(3t-1)}>0.\n$$\nThe inequality $2u\\le3a$ gives $\\rho\\le3/(3t-1)$, proving the claim. The first two terms alone would not prove this comparison. This is a sufficient exclusion of the current tail-mass deficit, not an exact test for membership in the remaining achievement set.*\n\n*The sufficient condition is weaker than $u\\le a$. A realizable example is $(k,u,L,a)=(2,7,13,5)$; it passes $2u\\le3a$ but not $u\\le a$. The linked scalar example $(u,a)=(3,2)$ proves strict containment of the inequalities, but is not integral rational data for this substitution. For comparison, the exact mass threshold is $a/u\\ge R_k^{-1}-(2^k-1)$; its right-hand side lies strictly between $0$ and $2/3$. None of these comparisons asserts that the half-greedy orbit satisfies the sufficient inequality at every skipped rank.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.record-257hg-i4","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.record-257hg-i4","id":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.record-257hg-i4%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_dyadic_skip_test_iff%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.record-257hg-i4%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_dyadic_skip_test_iff%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_dyadic_skip_test_iff"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.record-257hg-i4","id":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.record-257hg-i4%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_exact_mass_threshold%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.record-257hg-i4%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_exact_mass_threshold%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_exact_mass_threshold"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.record-257hg-i4","id":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.record-257hg-i4%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_sharp_gives_three_over_three_t_sub_one%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.record-257hg-i4%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_sharp_gives_three_over_three_t_sub_one%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to